  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1218 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe mid-level ridging will keep a persistent forecast in place for \nall of next week with continued rain free and hot weather across \nSouth-Central Texas. The ridge does slowly amplify and slightly \nnudge southward with time. This helps to tick the temperatures \nupward by a few degrees by the end of the week. However, afternoon \nheat indices don't budge much compared to the values within the \nshort term as diurnal mixing becomes a little more efficient. We'll \nmonitor those temperature and dew point trends, but for now the \nconditions are a little shy of the heat advisory criteria mid to \nlate next week. Otherwise, a light to moderate south-southeasterly \nflow maintains under mostly sunny/clear skies.",
